kpi Owner | Digital Channels
kpi Region | North Europe
kpi Last reviewed | 2026-09-22

## Overview

Passengers book through Azure Front Door. Every booking is written to one database and announced as an event, so the scanners at the terminals stay in step.

## Diagram

diagram ticketing dir=TB title="Ticketing platform on Azure"
ticketing: pax "Passengers" user
ticketing: fd "Front Door" ext
ticketing: pay "Payment Provider" ext
ticketing: scan "Port Terminal Scanners" ext
ticketing: web "Booking Web App" svc
ticketing: api "Ticketing API" svc focus
ticketing: db "Reservations DB" db "Azure SQL"
ticketing: events "Booking Events" queue "Service Bus"
ticketing: pax -> fd : HTTPS
ticketing: fd -> web : origin request
ticketing: web -> api : REST
ticketing: api -> db : SQL, port 1433
ticketing: api -> pay : card authorization
ticketing: api -> events : ticket issued
ticketing: events -> scan : sync every 30 s
ticketing: group appnet "App subnet (10.50.1.0/24)" web, api
ticketing: group datanet "Data subnet (10.50.2.0/24)" db, events
ticketing: group vnet "Ticketing VNet (10.50.0.0/16)" appnet, datanet
ticketing: group sub "Ticketing subscription" vnet

## Capacity

table = component,capacity; Booking Web App,"3 to 10 instances, scaling at 60 percent CPU"; Ticketing API,4 to 16 pods; Reservations DB,"8 vCores, with a read replica in the paired region"

## Recovery targets

kpi Recovery point objective | 5 minutes
kpi Recovery time objective | 1 hour
